      },
      "message": "fix(vector): handle xd==0 case correctly in vsetvli\n\nAccording to the RISC-V Vector spec, vsetvli has three cases:\n\n1. rs1 != x0: Normal stripmining - AVL from rs1, write vl to rd\n2. rs1 == x0, rd != x0: Set vl to VLMAX, write to rd\n3. rs1 == x0, rd == x0: Keep existing vl unchanged\n\nThe previous implementation only handled cases 1 and 2, always setting\nvl to VLMAX when xs1 == 0 regardless of xd.\n\nThis fix adds proper handling for case 3:\n- Save the old LMUL/SEW ratio before updating vtype\n- When xs1 == 0 && xd == 0, keep the existing vl value\n- If the LMUL/SEW ratio changes, set vill=1 and vl=0 (as per spec)\n\nThe fix aligns the IDL implementation with the Sail reference model\nwhich already correctly implements all three cases (lines 127-151 of\nthe sail() section).\n\nCloses #1269",
